## Best Practices for Environment Variables

### 1. Always Provide Defaults (but securely)
```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;

// ❌ BAD
const SECRET = process.env.JWT_SECRET;  // Crashes if not set in production
```

### 2. Validate Required Variables at Startup
```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
const JWT_SECRET = process.env.JWT_SECRET;
if (!JWT_SECRET && process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
  throw new Error('JWT_SECRET is required in production');
}

// ❌ BAD - Fails silently
const JWT_SECRET = process.env.JWT_SECRET || 'default-secret';
```

### 3. Use Descriptive Variable Names
```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS
RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS

// ❌ BAD
WINDOW
MAX
```

### 4. Type Conversion
```javascript
// ✅ GOOD - Explicit type conversion
const PORT = parseInt(process.env.PORT, 10) || 3000;
const MAX_CONNECTIONS = parseInt(process.env.MAX_CONNECTIONS) || 10;
const DEBUG_MODE = process.env.DEBUG_MODE === 'true';

// ❌ BAD - Type confusion
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;  // Will be string if set
```

### 5. Environment-Specific Defaults
```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
const LOG_LEVEL = process.env.LOG_LEVEL || 
  (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' ? 'error' : 'debug');

// ❌ BAD - Same default for all environments
const LOG_LEVEL = process.env.LOG_LEVEL || 'debug';
```

