## Issue #1: Server Port 🔴

**Location:** `app.js`, line 18

**Current Code:**
```javascript
app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});
```

**Problem:**
- Cannot run on different ports without editing code
- Breaks Docker/containerized deployments
- Prevents horizontal scaling

**Fixed Code:**
```javascript
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;
app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT}`);
});
```

**Usage:**
```bash
PORT=8000 node app.js    # Run on port 8000
PORT=3000 node app.js    # Run on port 3000
node app.js              # Use default 3000
```

---

## Issue #2: Server Host 🔴

**Location:** `app.js`, line 18 (implicit)

**Current Code:**
```javascript
app.listen(3000)  // Defaults to localhost
```

**Problem:**
- Won't accept external connections in Docker
- Breaks cloud deployments
- Only binds to localhost by default

**Fixed Code:**
```javascript
const HOST = process.env.HOST || 'localhost';
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;
app.listen(PORT, HOST, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on http://${HOST}:${PORT}`);
});
```

**Usage:**
```bash
HOST=0.0.0.0 PORT=3000 node app.js  # Docker/cloud
HOST=localhost PORT=3000 node app.js # Local dev
node app.js                           # Defaults
```

