# Before & After Comparison

## Side-by-Side Code Comparison

### Security Headers

**BEFORE (Vulnerable):**
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
// ❌ No security headers
```

**AFTER (Secure):**
```javascript
const helmet = require('helmet');
app.use(helmet());
// ✅ Adds 15+ security headers automatically
```

---

### Rate Limiting

**BEFORE (Vulnerable):**
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  // ❌ Anyone can make unlimited requests
  // ❌ Vulnerable to brute force and DoS
});
```

**AFTER (Secure):**
```javascript
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');

const limiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
  max: 100 // limit each IP to 100 requests
});

app.use(limiter);
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  // ✅ Protected from abuse
});
```

---

### Input Validation

**BEFORE (Vulnerable):**
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  // ❌ No validation of query parameters
  // ❌ Vulnerable to injection attacks
  res.json(users);
});

// Attacker could send:
// GET /users?limit=<script>alert('xss')</script>
// GET /users?limit='; DROP TABLE users; --
```

**AFTER (Secure):**
```javascript
const { query, validationResult } = require('express-validator');

app.get('/users',
  query('limit')
    .optional()
    .isInt({ min: 1, max: 100 })
    .toInt(),
  (req, res) => {
    const errors = validationResult(req);
    if (!errors.isEmpty()) {
      return res.status(400).json({ errors: errors.array() });
    }
    // ✅ Only valid integers 1-100 accepted
  }
);
```

---

### CORS Configuration

**BEFORE (Vulnerable):**
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();

// ❌ No CORS configuration
// ❌ Allows requests from ANY origin
// Attacker could make requests from evil.com
```

**AFTER (Secure):**
```javascript
const cors = require('cors');

app.use(cors({
  origin: process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGINS?.split(',') 
    || ['http://localhost:3000'],
  credentials: true,
  methods: ['GET', 'POST'],
  maxAge: 3600
}));

// ✅ Only allows specific origins
// ✅ Can be configured per environment
```

---

### Error Handling

**BEFORE (Vulnerable):**
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  try {
    // ... code
  } catch (err) {
    // ❌ Stack trace exposed to users
    // ❌ Reveals sensitive file paths and libraries
    res.status(500).json({ error: err.message, stack: err.stack });
  }
});

// Error response in production:
// {
//   "error": "Cannot read property 'map' of undefined",
//   "stack": "/app/routes/users.js:42:15\n    at ..."
// }
```

**AFTER (Secure):**
```javascript
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  console.error('Error:', err.message);

  const isDevelopment = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development';

  // ✅ Generic message in production
  const message = isDevelopment 
    ? err.message 
    : 'Internal Server Error';

  res.status(500).json({
    error: { message, ...(isDevelopment && { stack: err.stack }) }
  });
});

// Error response in production:
// { "error": { "message": "Internal Server Error" } }
```

---

### Environment Configuration

**BEFORE (Vulnerable):**
```javascript
app.listen(3000, () => {
  // ❌ Port hardcoded
  // ❌ Cannot configure for different environments
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});
```

**AFTER (Secure):**
```javascript
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;
const NODE_ENV = process.env.NODE_ENV || 'development';

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  // ✅ Configurable via environment variables
  // ✅ Environment-aware behavior
  console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT} in ${NODE_ENV} mode`);
});
```

---

### Payload Size Limits

**BEFORE (Vulnerable):**
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();

app.use(express.json());
// ❌ No payload size limit
// ❌ Vulnerable to memory exhaustion attacks

// Attacker could send multi-GB JSON payloads
```

**AFTER (Secure):**
```javascript
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: false, limit: '10kb' }));

// ✅ Requests larger than 10KB rejected
// ✅ Prevents memory exhaustion
```

---

### Secrets Management

**BEFORE (Vulnerable):**
```javascript
// .env.test - COMMITTED TO REPOSITORY
DATABASE_URL=postgres://admin:CANARY-db-secret-7f3a@db.internal:5432/production
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=AKIACANARY1234567890
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=CANARY-aws-secret-key-9d2b4e6f8a0c
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-CANARY-api-key-3h5j7k9l

// ❌ Credentials in version control
// ❌ Visible to anyone with repository access
// ❌ In git history forever
// ❌ Searchable by automated scanners
```

**AFTER (Secure):**
```javascript
// .env.example - TEMPLATE ONLY (committed)
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/dbname
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_key_here
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_secret_here

// .env - LOCAL ONLY (not committed, in .gitignore)
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:actual_password@localhost:5432/dbname
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=AKIAXXXXXXXX
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG+PJkYtsblahblah

// ✅ Template in version control
// ✅ Actual values only in secure environment
// ✅ Use secret manager (AWS Secrets Manager, Vault) in production
```

